WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
I am with Kevin Prince

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.260
and I'm going to teach him something that you might not know,

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.900
which is how to throw a bucket of water at someone.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:09.460
Yeah, you can have the bucket.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.680
All right, this is not if you want to actually drench someone

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:13.460
if you're angry at them,

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.760
but this is how you throw a bucket of water

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:16.100
if you are on stage.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:19.080
I got taught this by a pantomime dame

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.520
several years ago, when I was in panto.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.840
And the key thing is,

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.300
that what you would do normally to drench someone

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.600
is not what you want to do on stage,

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.960
because there's a big audience watching on YouTube or in the theater.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.880
And you want to go for dramatic effect

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.000
and you also don't want to soak through the costume.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.180
So, do you want to fill the bucket.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.380
Fill up the bucket.There we go!

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.280
About halfway.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.000
About halfway. There you go!

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.120
Yep! That's good,

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.180
because if you fill it too much,

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.800
then you're going to have too much momentum, you won't be able to heft it.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.160
Too little: it's not going to look good.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.660
So, you want to aim for the chin.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:50.540
This is the key.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.260
Bucket of water. Aim for the chin.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:53.120
Two reasons:

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.520
Number one, you hit him in the chest it's going to absolutely drench them,

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.100
which means dry out the costume, lots of time.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:00.980
Number two,

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.840
hit the chin, creates an enormous splash,

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.020
goes backwards, gives a brilliant show for the audience,

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.260
doesn't really get the person wet.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:09.140
--So, are you ready? --Yep!

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:09.640
Okay.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.540
It's been a while since I did this.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:12.040
You ready?

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:12.540
Yep.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.160
Aim for the chin. Go!

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:18.000
You missed!

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.000
Everything from here upwards is dry!

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.060
You...

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:25.340
Do you want to try that again?

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.980
Alright, fill it halfway.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:28.820
One.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:30.000
Two.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:30.840
Three.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.600
That is how you throw a bucket of water at some...

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:48.900
And that...

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:54.140
[water noise]

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.600
God dammit, Mel!

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.960
[Closed captions by MM.
